Lab 4: Configuring Clients to Use IdM
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure the IdM client software on a Linux system
Successfully join a client system to an existing IdM domain
Verify client authentication and user lookup functionality
Understand the client-server relationship in Identity Management
Troubleshoot common client configuration issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with system administration concepts
Knowledge of network connectivity and DNS resolution
Understanding of authentication concepts (users, groups, passwords)
Completion of previous IdM server setup labs or access to an existing IdM server
Root or sudo access on the client system
