Centralized Authentication: Users can log in to any IdM-joined system with their domain credentials
Unified Identity: User and group information is consistent across all systems
Enhanced Security: Centralized password policies and authentication mechanisms
Simplified Administration: User management from a single point of control
Scalability: Easy addition of new systems to the identity infrastructure
